1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,900
What was the book Alexander the Great kept under his pillow on every battlefield?

2
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:14,217
He ascended the throne at twenty and conquered from Greece to India,

3
00:00:14,217 --> 00:00:16,517
the greatest conqueror in history.

4
00:00:16,517 --> 00:00:19,567
Through years of relentless campaigning,

5
00:00:19,567 --> 00:00:21,950
he never marched without his books.

6
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:25,617
When I opened the Iliad,

7
00:00:25,617 --> 00:00:27,567
Achilles stood beside me.

8
00:00:27,567 --> 00:00:29,667
On the nights before battle,

9
00:00:29,667 --> 00:00:31,767
it was not my armor that kept me,

10
00:00:31,767 --> 00:00:33,417
it was the story.

11
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:37,850
That book was Homer's Iliad.

12
00:00:37,850 --> 00:00:44,400
Alexander carried a personal copy annotated by his tutor Aristotle throughout his entire campaign.

13
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:46,367
At the ruins of Troy,

14
00:00:46,367 --> 00:00:48,650
he laid a wreath at the tomb of Achilles.

15
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:50,600
At the plains of Gaugamela,

16
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:53,200
he charged at the head of his wedge formation,

17
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:56,667
writing his own epic in blood and glory.

18
00:00:58,567 --> 00:01:01,583
A hero's path begins on the battlefield,

19
00:01:01,583 --> 00:01:05,150
but his legend is completed in the pages of a book.

20
00:01:05,150 --> 00:01:08,300
If you want to know more, open my library.
